From edf0d37427db481cef675e06920b28f4a1149ffa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 20:13:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 110/194] feat: re-enable breakable cudagraph auto-enable on
 SM121 for DeepSeek-V4
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SM121 carve-out in _should_auto_enable_deepseek_v4_breakable_cudagraph was
added because breakable cudagraph produced garbage on trivial prompts on SM121.
That was upstream #45309 (reduced eager_break_during_capture), reverted upstream
in #45972 and now in our base. With the full @eager_break_during_capture split
restored, breakable cudagraph generates correctly on SM121 again -- verified on
2x GB10 (EP off): "2+2等于几" and arithmetic clean, throughput on-par-or-slightly-
better than FULL_AND_PIECEWISE (38.5 vs 36.7 out_tok/s). Drop the carve-out so
breakable auto-enables for DeepSeek-V4 on all SM12x platforms.

Signed-off-by: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
---
