Subject: [PATCH 132/194] perf(sm12x): drop per-step positions.max().item()
 device sync in C128A metadata
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

_c128a_effective_topk_width computed max_pos via int(positions.max().item()) —
a data-dependent device->host sync on the per-step C128A metadata build path
(build() -> _build_c128a_metadata, compress_ratio==128) that drains the launch
stream and kills CPU/GPU overlap every step (reported by wingcomm via gdb native
stacks on GB10/SM121).

Source max_pos from CommonAttentionMetadata.max_seq_len instead (already computed
CPU-side, no sync); use (max_seq_len - 1). effective_topk is a 128-aligned ceiling
clamped to max_compressed_tokens, so an upper bound only rounds the width up within
the same finite {128..8192} set — buffer- and JIT-set-safe. For decode max_seq_len-1
== positions.max() exactly; only chunked prefill sees a (safe) slightly-wider width.
Keeps a positions.max() fallback when max_seq_len is unavailable.

