From 2a9a806f282d50e782eb926c7413d2f39be2b675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 21:30:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 133/194] fix(weight-loader): only set `yielded` after a tensor
 is emitted (GDS fallback)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In fastsafetensors_weights_iterator's GDS try-path, `yielded` was set at the top
of the loop, before the EP/name skip check — so a leading tensor filtered out by
local_expert_ids / weight_name_filter falsely marked the stream as "yielded". A
lazy GDS RuntimeError after such a skipped tensor (but before the first kept one)
then re-raised instead of falling back to nogds=True, even though nothing had been
emitted and restarting is safe. Move `yielded = True` after the skip, next to the
actual yield, matching the documented intent. (Codex review on c766cbc6ff.)

Signed-off-by: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
---
