From 78e0a1bb4a4cb5897a47cbfdbca998e1de386ffa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 06:23:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 136/194] fix(sm12x): warm full D512-split prefill width range
 to avoid first-prefill JIT

The D512-split sparse-MLA prefill kernels are JIT-keyed on the per-request
combined_topk width. C4 indexer layers use the static topk_bound+window (~640
for DSv4-Flash), but the C128A layer (compress_ratio=128) uses a context-
dependent effective_topk that grows in 128-aligned steps up to the split
ceiling, so a long-context prefill sweeps widths 768..1152. The warmup capped at
the static C4 bound, leaving 768..1152 (4 widths x 3 kernels = 12 compiles) to
JIT in-inference on the first long request (~20s spike; reported via
jasl/vllm#23). Warm the full split range [256..1152]; the runtime workspace
already sizes to the actual per-request width, so correctness is unchanged.

Validated on GB10 2-node TP=2 (mnbt=512, MTP=2, fp8 KV): D512-split
JIT-in-inference 24 -> 0 on a 60k-token prefill; +~6s startup warmup;
KV-cache/peak memory unchanged; sampled outputs correct.

Signed-off-by: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
