From 367ed7c662c3097a5633126f8fb0083b8bb8b716 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 01:07:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 139/194] fix(sm12x): address Codex P2 findings (NVFP4 scale
 load, DSML non-stream, C128A KV slots)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three real P2s from the Codex review on PR #41834:

- routed_experts: restore RoutedExperts._to_scalar staticmethod. The 06-26
  reconcile merge dropped it but left a live caller in the ModelOpt NVFP4 w1/w3
  input-scale branch plus two unit tests, so loading a ModelOpt NVFP4 MoE
  checkpoint raised AttributeError on weight load.

- deepseek_v4 reasoning parser: override the non-streaming extract_reasoning so a
  thinking-mode completion emitting <｜DSML｜tool_calls> WITHOUT </think> splits at
  the marker (reasoning before; marker+rest as content) instead of inheriting the
  base </think>-only split (which returned content=None and dropped the tool
  call). Mirrors the existing streaming logic. +4 unit tests.

- flashinfer_sm120_decode: convert C128A packed-prefill topk indices to global KV
  slots (+ lens) via the block table, mirroring the C4 branch. They were passed
  through as per-request-local positions, so the paged runner read wrong KV
  blocks for req>0 / non-contiguous layouts. Gated behind
  VLLM_DEEPSEEK_V4_FLASHINFER_SM120_DECODE (off by default).

The 4th Codex P2 (llm_base_proposer seeded generators) was already fixed in
76dff54c23. CPU unit tests pass (24 reasoning + 2 _to_scalar). The C128A path is
gated off by default and needs the FI-decode path for end-to-end validation.

Signed-off-by: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
