From 9bccfd13887d19363f6dacd8bfd3c8b598469043 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 04:51:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 154/194] fix(sm12x): exact non-cooperative persistent_topk for
 <128KB-smem parts (GB10)

persistent_topk's cooperative-radix "large" path (seq_len > RADIX_THRESHOLD)
needs all ctas_per_group CTAs co-resident for a spin-wait barrier; ctas_per_group
grows with context and past num_sms*occupancy it falls back to FilteredTopK,
which needs >=128KB smem/block. GB10 (SM121) and consumer Blackwell (RTX SM120/
50-series) expose ~99KB opt-in smem -> hard fail at ~400k context (reproduced:
total_ctas=49 @ stride 400k > 48). The co-residency spin-wait barrier is also
fragile under a CUDA-graph-captured NCCL collective (community 4-node hang).

Fix: gate on smem CAPACITY (max_smem_per_block < 128KB), not capability family
(RTX 50-series is also family-120). On such parts force ctas_per_group=1 +
needs_cooperative=false (no barrier), and route every row through a single-CTA,
barrier-free selector: trivial / histogram_2048 / histogram_256 for seq_len <=
RADIX_THRESHOLD (unchanged status quo), and a NEW histogram_streaming_topk for
long rows.

histogram_streaming_topk is an exact 4-round MSD radix that re-streams the row
from global each round (filtered by the accumulated prefix) with a strict pivot
convention, then a streaming collection -- it never buffers equal-to-threshold
candidates (histogram_256_topk's bounded MAX_BUFFERED_ITEMS buffer overflows at
dense long-context pivots and under-selects). Validated bit-exact vs torch.topk
and vs the cooperative path on GB10 across 128k-640k context, topk 512/2048,
multi-row. ~3KB smem, no per-row cap.

Removes both the long-context hard-fail and the cooperative barrier on GB10.
>=128KB devices (Hopper, datacenter Blackwell) are byte-identical (all changes
guarded by force_noncooperative). Debug escape hatch: VLLM_TOPK_DISABLE_NONCOOP=1.
---
