From b9980bdf79ec61e53a84a0ac931f11fde1c66ab6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 12:55:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 164/194] deepseek_v4: honor MTP-layer compress_ratio=0
 (unscaled draft rope)

Port of vllm-project/vllm#48304. Our fork carried the exact pre-fix code:
draft layers (layer_id >= num_hidden_layers) were forced to compress_ratio=1
with yarn-scaled rope, ignoring DSpark checkpoints whose compress_ratios
include the MTP draft layer with entry 0 (uncompressed KV + plain rope).

- resolve_layer_compress_ratio(config, layer_id) -> (max(1,entry), entry==0);
  operational ratio stays >=1 (unchanged for the draft), entry 0 only flips
  rope selection to plain/unscaled.
- rope.py: dict()-copy rope_parameters (no shared-config mutation), select
  rope_type='default' under the flag, pin cos_sin_cache dtype=fp32 (DSv4
  kernels assert fp32; the plain-rope path previously inherited bf16 default).
- adds tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_rope.py (CPU-only).

Measured upstream: draft acceptance 57%->69%, pos-2 0.275->0.50. No KV-cache
layout change (draft operational ratio stays 1).
