From cfddacbc47be28913ec1522fdc1e1b5f972bb438 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:27:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 167/194] fix(deepseek_v4): honor eagle +1 in SWA-MLA
 prefix-cache block protection

SlidingWindowMLAManager.cache_blocks inlined cdiv(sliding_window - 1,
block_size) without the eagle +1 that find_longest_cache_hit's
_contiguous_blocks_for_hit requires. Under MTP/eagle the last prompt-suffix
block was left unprotected; once the block pool churned it evicted, the SWA
probe returned 0, and the hybrid coordinator's per-group min zeroed the entire
prefix-cache hit -> hit rate flips to exactly 0% and stays there. Use the shared
helper so protection matches the hit path; non-eagle behavior unchanged.

Also rename the stale max_num_batched_tokens= kwarg to max_in_flight_tokens= in
the DeepSeek-V4 MLA prefix-cache tests: the upstream sync renamed that
KVCacheManager param, but the fork tests still passed the old name -> TypeError.

Reported with root-cause + reproducer by @calper-ql (vllm-project/vllm#41834).

Signed-off-by: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
