From 7314ceaa11ea268d66cf7c067397c530b6cb729c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 06:16:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 191/194] Cherry-pick vllm-project/vllm#49335: swizzle mxfp8
 activation scales after DP/EP dispatch

FLASHINFER_CUTLASS_MXFP4_MXFP8 returns NaN logits for every request when
data_parallel_size > 1, silently: the server stays healthy and generates at
full speed while completions decode to empty strings.

The DP/EP prepare paths quantize with row-major scales so they can ride the
a2a next to the hidden states and swizzle afterwards, but that restore step
only handled nvfp4 -- mxfp8 scales reached the CUTLASS kernel row-major and it
read wrong e8m0 block exponents. Our tree has the same gap
(naive_dp_ep.py gated the restore on quant_dtype == "nvfp4").

Inert for GB10, which runs data_parallel_size=1: at DP=1 the scales are
quantized directly into the swizzled layout, which is why the existing tests
never caught this. Taken for the multi-node DP users of this branch.
Upstream PR is still open and untouched since 2026-07-21.
