From b68ecd479ca6c29ba36601d6cb00053c6b4fccfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasl <jasl9187@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 22:18:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 192/194] Cherry-pick vllm-project/vllm#50686: merge
 consecutive assistant messages

Clients that replay agentic tool-calling history commonly split one logical
assistant turn into two consecutive assistant messages -- a content-only
preamble followed by tool_calls + reasoning. encode_messages only emits the
Assistant transition after user/developer messages, so the second message is
glued onto the first with no separator.

Reproduced here before taking it (drop_thinking=False, DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731):

  before: <|Assistant|><think></think>CONTENT<|end_of_sentence|>REASONING</think>
  after:  <|Assistant|><think>REASONING</think>CONTENT

The reasoning rendered as free text with no opener and a stray closing think
tag. Our default drop_thinking=True path benefits too, in a way the upstream
description does not call out: it drops a spurious mid-turn end-of-sentence
that was splitting one logical turn into two EOS-terminated blocks.

  before: <|Assistant|></think>CONTENT<|end_of_sentence|>
  after:  <|Assistant|></think>CONTENT

Orthogonal to our local delta in this file (defensive handling of empty/None
tool_call arguments). Test file kept both sides; tests/tokenizers_ is 44 passed.
Upstream PR is open and unlikely to be picked up soon.
